\description{
\ifelse{html}{\href{https://lifecycle.r-lib.org/articles/stages.html#experimental}{\figure{lifecycle-experimental.svg}{options: alt='[Experimental]'}}}{\strong{[Experimental]}}
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=list_sp_list_views]{list_sp_list_views()}} lists the views for a SharePoint list.
\item \code{\link[=get_sp_list_view]{get_sp_list_view()}} gets a single view by title or ID (or the default
view).
\item \code{\link[=create_sp_list_view]{create_sp_list_view()}} creates a view.
\item \code{\link[=update_sp_list_view]{update_sp_list_view()}} updates a view. Only properties that differ from
the existing view are changed.
\item \code{\link[=delete_sp_list_view]{delete_sp_list_view()}} deletes a view. The default view can't be deleted.
}

The Graph API doesn't support list views, so these functions use the
SharePoint REST API and require a delegated (user) login with a refresh
token, such as the default Microsoft365R login. View properties use the
SharePoint REST API
\href{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/office/sharepoint-csom/jj244979(v=office.15)}{SP.View}
property names (e.g. \code{ViewFields} or \code{RowLimit}) and the arguments use the
same names in snake case (e.g. \code{view_fields} or \code{row_limit}).
}
\details{
View queries

\code{view_query} is a \href{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sharepoint/dev/schema/query-schema}{CAML}
query with optional \verb{<Where>}, \verb{<OrderBy>}, and \verb{<GroupBy>} elements (but
without an enclosing \verb{<Query>} element). Reference columns by internal name.
For example, to show active items sorted by amount:

\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode">}}\preformatted{<Where><Eq><FieldRef Name="Status"/><Value Type="Choice">Active</Value></Eq></Where>
<OrderBy><FieldRef Name="Amount" Ascending="FALSE"/></OrderBy>
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

Limitations
\itemize{
\item Board, gallery, and calendar views can be listed but their layout
settings can't be changed.
\item Personal views can be listed but not created.
\item Hidden views include list form settings (e.g. a hidden "Untitled Form"
view holds custom form formatting) and are excluded by default.
\item Changing view fields removes and re-adds every field. If a request fails
partway through, call \code{\link[=update_sp_list_view]{update_sp_list_view()}} again.
\item Renaming a view doesn't change the view URL.
}
